Z||000000||Kelvin Vivian||04-12-2001||11:14 PM||||What happened to that Fiero Email List Serve thing-a-ma-bob that was going on around 1994-whenever? When did it end?<P>I ran across Rodney Sizemore's website (one of the original Fiero websites)  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.org</A>  and I was reminded of that earlier "forum"... Lots of great Fiero information was passed during that time as it is in this forum. Rodney has a "Who's Who of Fiero owners" on the website and I have an entry there, my entry was posted when I was driving my first fiero, a white 1985 SE.<P>The first Fiero website I came across on the WWW was one created by Peter Zurich (I think) it had a red 85 GT on its front page, and this was around 1992-1993... The website no longer exists. Cliff has done an excellent job in continuing the tradition of great Fiero websites...||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||04-12-2001||11:23 PM||||Its still going on, I subscribe in digest mode, usually I just delete them because there's never anything interesting.  Oh BTW its no longer moderated, I think it stopped around '99...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">    <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||1
